A||N||5||bHooper||cruise servo vacuum line question||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||01-24-2001||09:27 PM||||i decided to check the fluid level in my tranny, and when i reached for the dipstick, i heard a hiss.<P>i looked at the vacuum lines going to the cruise control, and they are extremely rotten.  where do these led to?  it looks as if they go to that ugly canister (coffee can) underneath the servo.  what purpose does that serve?<P>could these be the reason that my cruise hasn't worked in 11 years?  will it cause any problems, if i dont fix them right away?<P>what about the canister?  what is that for, and how often should it be replaced?<P>the haynes, and clymer books dont talk about these, so i had to ask.  <P>oh yeah, and my car is a '86GT 5spd, and wasn't running at the time.<P>thanks!<BR>hoop<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000001||DJRice||01-24-2001||09:45 PM||||Rodney Dickman sells copies of the cruise diagnostic pages for $6 that will help troubleshoot pretty much any problem.  The vacuum driven servo is what pulls on your throttle body to vary the throttle.  Vacuum leaks as a whole can do pretty goofy things to these engines.  Things may be ok today, but tomorrow who knows what could go awry.  <P>It could very well be that the rotten vacuum hoses are the cause of your cruise woes.  I am not sure if you need to clean the vacuum canister, but as long as it is intact is should be able to do its job.  <P>Vacuum lines are cheap, it cant hurt to replace them then go for a ride to see what happens.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||01-24-2001||10:43 PM||||ok i understand replaceing the lines, but what does the canister do?||||reg||1
Z||000003||wkayl||01-24-2001||11:01 PM||||It gives you a vacum reserve for when you are at open throttle.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/outline.jpg">   <BR>86GT original paint, interior, engine  <A HREF="http://www.fierowayne.homestead.com/fierowayne.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierowayne.homestead.com/fierowayne.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||01-25-2001||07:31 PM||||While you are messing with it replace the metal can. Those things almost always leak at this age. There are notes in my cave's engine area about vac leaks and the can and what you can replace it with.<P>the can needs to be there. It does what wkayl said. the cruise will not work right without it.||||reg||1
